-- title:
--   Principal-series map from split tame inertia labels at q
-- statement:
--   Let $M\ge 1$, let $g$ be a weight-two cusp form on $\Gamma_0(M)$ which is a newform (a normalised eigenform none of whose proper level divisors carries a cusp form matching its $q$-coefficients away from $M$), let $\lambda$ be a prime and $S$ a finite set of naturals, and let $\mathcal O'$ be a characteristic-zero complete discrete valuation domain with finite residue field in which $\lambda$ lies in the maximal ideal, with $\lambda\neq 2$. Let $\chi_g$ be a ring homomorphism from the Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra M 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) to $\mathbb C$ sending each $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell\nmid M$, $\ell\notin S$) to the $\ell$-th $q$-coefficient of $g$, let $\iota$ map the range of $\chi_g$ into $\mathcal O'$, and let $\rho$ be a rank-two adically continuous $\mathcal O'$-representation of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ whose residual representation is irreducible and odd (every element of order two has determinant $-1$) and which satisfies, at every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ over such an $\ell$ and every Frobenius element $\sigma$ at $\ell$ for $A$, $\mathrm{charpoly}(\rho(\sigma))=X^2-\iota\chi_g(T_\ell)X+\ell$. Let $q\neq\lambda$ be a prime with $M.\mathrm{factorization}\,q=2$, let $\Phi\neq 0$ be an adelic lift of $g$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the adeles of $\mathbb Q$, and let $P$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ in its nonunits such that $\rho(\sigma)=1$ for every $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup of $P$ over $\mathbb Q$ with $\sigma z\,z^{-1}-1$ a nonunit of $P$ for all $z\neq 0$. Assume finally that there are an injective ring homomorphism $j:\mathcal O'\to\mathcal O''$ into a domain and a map $a$ from the Galois group to $(\mathcal O'')^\times$ such that, for $\sigma$ in that inertia subgroup, $j$ carries $\mathrm{charpoly}(\rho(\sigma))$ to $(X-a(\sigma))(X-a(\sigma)^{-1})$, that $a$ is multiplicative on the inertia subgroup, and that $a(\sigma)^{q-1}=1$ there. Then there exist homomorphisms $\mu_1,\mu_2:\mathbb Q_q^\times\to\mathbb C^\times$ and a non-zero $\mathbb C$-linear, $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb Q_q)$-equivariant map from the span of the adelic translates of $\Phi$ to the principal-series space of locally constant functions on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb Q_q)$ transforming under the Borel by $\mu_1\otimes\mu_2$ times the half-modulus.
--
--   This is the local statement at $q$ in the analysis of a newform of level exactly divisible by $q^2$: tame inertia at $q$ acting through $\rho$ with split, $(q-1)$-torsion eigenvalue labels forces the automorphic representation generated by an adelic lift to admit a non-zero equivariant map to a principal series. It is used in contrapositive form by the companion result which, from the vanishing of all such principal-series maps, produces inertia characteristic polynomials whose labels fail to be $(q-1)$-torsion.
